          "code": "GOLDEN_ANSWER",
          "id": "1774386881179",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774386881180_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your entire knowledge is limited to the following references.\nDo not use any other information to perform the task.\n  \n## reference content\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.context}}\n \n## question\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.question}}\n  \nGiven the question and reference content above perform the following instructions:\n1. Understand the question.\n- Carefully read and interpret the question to grasp the main intent and specific details.\n- Restate the question in your own words.\n- Example rephrasing for input question \"make kubernetes cluster in OCI\":\n```\nHow can I create a kubernetes cluster in OCI?\n```\n- Let REPHRASED_QUESTION be that question.\n\n2. Analyze the Provided Reference Content\n- Review the reference content. \n- Identify and extract the most relevant information that directly addresses the question.\n\n3. Construct a Clear and Concise Response\n- Synthesize the extracted information into a well-structured answer.\n- Format the answer using paragraphs.\n- Use at least {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.sizeLowerBound}} words. Use at most {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.sizeUpperBound}} words.\n- Use clear and straightforward language in a professional tone to ensure the response is easily understandable.\n- Maintain objectivity and avoid inserting personal opinions.\n\n4. Ensure Completeness and Relevance\n- Address all aspects of the question.\n- Avoid including unrelated information that might confuse the user who asked the question.\n\n5. Review for Accuracy and Clarity\n- Proofread the response to eliminate any errors or ambiguities.\n- Make sure the answer fully satisfies the question based on the available reference content.\n\n6. Language\n- Generate the answer in the `{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.locale}}` locale.\n\n7. Generate the answer\n- Let ANSWER be your answer to the question.\n- Example answer for question: \"How can I create a kubernetes cluster in OCI?\"\n```\nI understand that you are looking for how to create a cluster in OCI.\n\nTo create a cluster, you need to follow these steps:\n1. Sign in to the Oracle Cloud Infrastructure Console.\n2. Navigate to Developer Services and select Kubernetes Clusters (OKE).\n3. Click 'Create Cluster' and choose 'Quick Create'.\n4. Provide a name, compartment, and other required details.\n5. Review the settings and click 'Create Cluster'.\n6. Wait for the cluster to be created, which may take a few minutes.\n```\n\n8. Put the question interpretation and answer into the JSON format:\n{\n    \"user_intent\": \"<REPHRASED_QUESTION>\",\n    \"answer\": \"<ANSWER>\"\n}\n\n---\n\n**Usage Tips:**\n\n- **Stay Objective:** Base all responses strictly on the provided articles without adding personal insights.\n\n- **Be Transparent:** If the reference content does not provide relevant information that directly addresses the user's question, you must answer only with \"n/a\".\n\n- **Maintain Professionalism:** Use a respectful and informative tone tailored to the user's needs.\n\nBy following this prompt structure, you can ensure that responses are accurate, relevant, and effectively utilize the content from top search result articles to address end-user questions."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
